@page "/docs/components/sortable"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Sortable
<PageTitle>Sortable - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Sortable</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="sortable" />
        </div>
        <p>Reorder or swap items with a pointer or entirely from the keyboard, in a vertical column, a horizontal row or a wrapping grid. Every committed move is reported as a <span class="font-mono text-sm">SortableChange</span> that you apply to your own data. Lists that share a group can also pass items to one another.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(SortableUsageExample)"
                Description="Bind a list to `BzSortableList` and give it an item template, or compose `BzSortableItem` children under `BzSortable`. Handle `OnReorder`, or bind `Items`, to keep the new order." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="A sortable holds its items, and an optional handle inside an item limits dragging to that grip." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="Drag an item to a new place in the list. From the keyboard, Tab to an item, press Space to pick it up, move it with the arrow keys and press Space again to drop it." Example="typeof(SortableDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Drag handle" Description="With a `BzSortableHandle` inside an item, only the grip starts a drag and shows the grab cursor. The rest of the item stays clickable." Example="typeof(SortableHandleExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Data-driven" Description="`BzSortableList` renders one keyed item per element of the bound list and applies each move to it for you." Example="typeof(SortableDataExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Horizontal" Description="Set `Orientation` to `Horizontal` to lay items out in a row, where chips of different widths make room by their own size. `LockAxis` keeps the drag on the row, and a picked-up item moves with the Left and Right arrow keys." Example="typeof(SortableHorizontalExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Grid" Description="`Orientation.Grid` tracks the drop target in two dimensions. Pass `Columns` so the Up and Down arrow keys move an item a whole row." Example="typeof(SortableGridExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Swap" Description="Set `Strategy` to `Swap` to trade the dragged item with the one you drop it on. `SwapMode` picks the preview: `Swap`, the default, trades places live as you hover, while `Drop` holds everything still until release, so pair it with `ShowPlaceholder` to keep the target visible." Example="typeof(SortableSwapExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Mixed-size grid" Description="Cards can span columns and rows. While you drag, every card moves to the exact place it will land, because the candidate order is laid out in a hidden measurement pass first, and the placeholder marks where the dragged card goes." Example="typeof(SortableMixedGridExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Animations" Description="`Animation` picks the motion: `Dynamic` for a quick glide (the default), `Spring` for a bouncy overshoot, or `None` for instant moves. When the operating system asks for reduced motion, items snap instantly whatever you choose." Example="typeof(SortableAnimationsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Cross-list groups" Description="Give two lists the same `Group` to drag items between them. Each list also has an `Id`, so the handler can tell the source from the target." Example="typeof(SortableCrossExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Transfer control" Description="`AllowTransferOut` and `AllowTransferIn` control cross-list moves for each list, and setting `AllowSorting` to `false` stops reordering within one. Here the palette only gives items away, and the canvas takes them in through its own `OnReceive` handler." Example="typeof(SortableTransferExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom cursors" Description="`Cursor` and `GrabbingCursor` take any CSS cursor value, and `BzCursor.From` turns a Blaizio icon into one, here an open and a closed hand. Set them once on the list and every item and handle uses them." Example="typeof(SortableCursorsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Keyboard & accessibility" Description="Every sortable works from the keyboard. Tab to an item and press Space to pick it up, move it with the arrow keys, then press Space to drop or Escape to cancel. A live region announces the pick-up, the drop and a cancel." Example="typeof(SortableKeyboardExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzSortable",
        new CompositionNode("BzSortableItem",
            new CompositionNode("BzSortableHandle")),
        new CompositionNode("BzSortableItem"));
}
